[{"id":129696,"q":"This implies that in the long run a sustained improvement in the growth scenario through monetary financing of the deficit could involve a severe trade-off in terms of inflation - every one per cent additional output growth implies nearly 6 to 6.5 per cent rise in inflation rate in the long run.","sp":"Bimal Jalan","ss":"bimal-jalan","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-28 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":0.35,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["inflation","growth","fiscal","trade"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970203b.pdf","v":""},{"id":129720,"q":"It recorded a seasonally-adjusted annual rate of 1.82 million starts in October 1996, the highest level since November 1973, partly reflecting the increase in orders in September 1996 before the expected rise in the consumption tax.","sp":"Bank of Japan","ss":"bank-of-japan","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-20 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":36,"p":0.7,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["fiscal"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970107b.pdf","v":""},{"id":252446,"q":"requires state ownership in all banks to be less than 25 per cent by the end","sp":"European Commission","ss":"european-commission","in":"European Commission","c":"EU","t":"1996-12-19 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":null,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["finance"],"u":"https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/speech_96_337","v":""},{"id":252445,"q":"This year, however, there will be little daylight","sp":"European Commission","ss":"european-commission","in":"European Commission","c":"EU","t":"1996-12-19 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"oracular","tl":"Partly testable","am":36,"p":0.85,"h":"1996-12-31","st":"due","stl":"Due - being checked","tp":[],"u":"https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/speech_96_337","v":""},{"id":252444,"q":"which will give trade a further boost from the beginning of next year by","sp":"European Commission","ss":"european-commission","in":"European Commission","c":"EU","t":"1996-12-19 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"oracular","tl":"Partly testable","am":36,"p":0.85,"h":"1997-12-31","st":"due","stl":"Due - being checked","tp":["trade"],"u":"https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/speech_96_337","v":""},{"id":129714,"q":"If, for example, the bank's balance sheet is less than transparent, potential investors or creditors, seeing the nominally high 10 percent capital, but not recognizing that the economic risk capital allocation should, in percentage terms, be much higher, could direct an inappropriately high level of scarce resources toward the bank.","sp":"Alice M Rivlin","ss":"alice-m-rivlin","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-19 00:00","a":"combination","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":0.35,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["finance"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970108b.pdf","v":""},{"id":129707,"q":"The twelve-month price increase thus resumed its pre-August 1995 trend and will be less than 2% at the end of 1996, in line with the objective set by the Monetary Policy Council.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":36,"p":0.85,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["interest rates"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970115a.pdf","v":""},{"id":129706,"q":"This figure is consistent with price inflation of no more than 2% and non-inflationary real GDP growth of about 2.5%, which could be exceeded, in view of the potential for growth to catch up in the medium term.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"forecast","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":0.35,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["inflation","growth"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970115a.pdf","v":""},{"id":129705,"q":"3. -An intermediate internal growth target for the money supply assessed by the development of the narrow and broad monetary aggregates: in 1997, the money supply should be able to show a medium-term growth trend of 5%.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"combination","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":null,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["growth"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970115a.pdf","v":""},{"id":129704,"q":"The objective of the Monetary Policy Council is that the increase in prices, as measured by the consumer price index, should not exceed 2% in 1997. as in the medium term.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"combination","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":null,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["inflation","interest rates"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970115a.pdf","v":""},{"id":129703,"q":"4. -An intermediate internal growth target for the money supply as assessed by the development of the narrow and broad monetary aggregates: in 1997, the money supply should be able to show a medium-term growth trend of 5%.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"combination","ax":"empirical","tl":"Partly testable","am":56,"p":null,"h":null,"st":"open","stl":"Not due yet","tp":["growth"],"u":"https://www.bis.org/review/r970115a.pdf","v":""},{"id":129702,"q":"The objective of the Monetary Policy Council is that the increase in prices, as measured by the consumer price index, should not exceed 2% in 1997, as in the medium term.","sp":"Bank of France","ss":"bank-of-france","in":"Central bank (via BIS)","c":"INT","t":"1996-12-17 00:00","a":"combination","ax":"empirical","tl"